-- Rank ties (spec §15 / ex38): the blessed dense value-only rank write-back on tied Gold. Twin of s13-rank-ties.bqn.
-- Three units, two purses tied at 5. Equal values must take equal ranks — rank is a function of the value, not of the row that happens to hold it.
-- On gold 5 5 3 the tied pair shares a rank: 1 1 0 (value-only; the ¯1 sentinel init is fully overwritten — all rows are Unit).
-- The .bqn is half decision record: its ordinal-rank branch (⍋⍋gold -> 1 2 0, the retired "ties are stable" reading)
-- and the Sym(I)-equivariance permutation check (p = 1 0 2 swaps the tied pair) have NO ano surface and stay in the .bqn twin;
-- the equivariance fact is pinned at fixture level: permuting rows 0,1 leaves gold bitwise identical, so Rank must come out identical.
--! registry ../registries/s13-rank-ties.reg
--! expect rank = 1 1 0

Unit , Rank = rank(Gold)
